.Dd November 14, 2026
.Dt XCODE-SELECT 1
.Os MiniDarwin
.Sh NAME
.Nm xcode-select
.Nd print or change the active developer directory
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl h | Fl p | Fl r | Fl v | Fl -install | Fl s Ar path
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The active developer directory decides which developer tools the commands
in
.Pa /usr/bin
(such as
.Xr cc 1 ,
.Xr make 1
and
.Xr xcrun 1 )
run: an Xcode's
.Pa Contents/Developer ,
or a Command Line Tools installation.
.Pp
It is, in order: the
.Ev DEVELOPER_DIR
environment variable; the link
.Pa /var/select/developer_dir ;
the link
.Pa /var/db/xcode_select_link ;
the link
.Pa /usr/share/xcode-select/xcode_dir_link ;
the path in
.Pa /usr/share/xcode-select/xcode_dir_path ;
and otherwise the first of
.Pa /Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer ,
.Pa /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools
and
.Pa /Applications/Xcode-beta.app/Contents/Developer
that has
.Pa usr/lib/libxcrun.dylib .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage and exit.
.It Fl p , Fl -print-path
Print the active developer directory.
.It Fl s Ar path , Fl -switch Ar path
Make
.Ar path
the active developer directory: an Xcode application, its
.Pa Contents/Developer ,
a Command Line Tools directory, or a volume root.
Must be run as root.
.It Fl r , Fl -reset
Remove the setting, returning to the default.
Must be run as root.
.It Fl -install
Install the Command Line Tools.
An installer agent is asked first; with none,
.Pa /usr/libexec/xcselect-install
is run, which shows Apple's licence and installs the newest release for this
system from Apple's Software Update service.
.It Fl v , Fl -version
Print the version.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on a usage or permission error, 2 when no developer
directory can be found or a link cannot be written.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xcrun 1 ,
.Xr mdpkg 8
